{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Bedrock embedding entitlement — measured, and it splits in two.\n\nThe epic's certified round-4 finding recorded that `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` scopes `bedrock:InvokeModel` to `anthropic.claude-*` only, with no embedding ARN, and concluded candidate 3 may have to be recorded `unavailable`. Measuring it shows the constraint is real but narrower than that, and candidate 3 IS measurable.\n\nMeasured from the operator identity that runs the eval harness\n(`arn:aws:iam::896586841071:user/joe_frontier`), region `us-west-2`:\n\n- `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` — OK, dim 1024\n- `amazon.titan-embed-text-v1` — OK, dim 1536\n- `cohere.embed-english-v3` — OK, dim 1024\n\nConfirmed the policy text at `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf:64-66`; its resource list is exactly:\n\n    arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/anthropic.claude-*\n    arn:aws:bedrock:*:<acct>:inference-profile/*.anthropic.claude-*\n\nSo both statements hold, about different principals:\n\n1. The **eval harness** runs under an operator identity and CAN call Titan. Candidate 3 is measurable, so AC2's \"all three candidates\" is satisfiable without an `unavailable` row.\n2. The **review-bot instance role** (`rebar-gerrit-instance-role`) is scoped to Anthropic Claude and CANNOT call an embedding model. Adopting a vector architecture requires adding an embedding ARN to `iam_s7.tf`.\n\nThat second point is a deployment precondition, and the ADR will record it as one rather than as a measurement gap.\n\nScope note on the evidence: `iam_s7.tf:30-38` explicitly warns that entitlement must be re-verified from the instance and \"never from an operator identity holding bedrock:*\" — which is exactly what the test above used. It is therefore evidence about the eval path only. It does not show the instance role can call Titan, and I am not claiming it does; the instance-role scoping above comes from reading the policy, not from simulation.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793501291335574036,"uuid":"5c5ee102-4a0e-49fe-bb29-942ddc0bbdca"}